    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T1H1N1A1",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped 'Logic Gate NOT-NAND' gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: first XOR stage of stage 1's partial sum (chain 1 of 10), Y = NAND(A1, B1), feeding T1H1N21.B. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate's truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction — there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages — and each stage's carry-out, which must reach the next stage's several carry-in pins — are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in 'Logic Gate Half Adder').",
        "Identifier": "group_ab9dd945121a4b8080a8f569ef794a26",
        "IdGuid": "9d0ee4dd-4a53-448b-ba3f-0f2c817928ce",
        "ChildComponentGuids": [
