    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T1H1CARRYC3",
        "Description": "NOT reading (input A, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.375) of the shipped 'Logic Gate NOT-NAND' gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: carry-OR copy 3 of stage 1: Y = A1 AND B1, feeding T1ORNOT1C3.A. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate's truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction — there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages — and each stage's carry-out, which must reach the next stage's several carry-in pins — are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in 'Logic Gate Half Adder').",
        "Identifier": "group_f6265cdaba544b46a3ff31c0ce9bb17e",
        "IdGuid": "c9f47ef9-ec0e-4798-8c84-334f2ad339da",
