    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T2H1N1A4",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped 'Logic Gate NOT-NAND' gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: first XOR stage of stage 2's partial sum (chain 4 of 7), Y = NAND(A2, B2), feeding T2H1N24.B. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate's truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction — there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages — and each stage's carry-out, which must reach the next stage's several carry-in pins — are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in 'Logic Gate Half Adder').",
        "Identifier": "group_2ef93ac17a8f4797ab7b33c1812e74c3",
        "IdGuid": "d1736c45-a2b0-4439-89d7-58184c91fc2f",
